From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:56:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Specifications: re-observe the exact Lean release and
 dependencies after the last Lean run

Both execute() paths (lean_statements_20261010, lean_statement_proofs_20261011)
now call final_observation() after the negative controls and the post
source_check equality: `lake env lean --version` again (log version-final),
held to the pinned release and to the preflight line exactly, and
dependency_state() again, held to the preflight revisions and clean
worktrees. Any difference fails closed before a receipt is written. The
receipt keeps lean_version, dependency_revisions and dependency_worktrees
and adds observations = {preflight, final}.

New FinalObservation tests drive execute() with check.run replaced by a fake
(no Lean is started) and real disposable git checkouts as dependencies:
final version differs, a dependency HEAD moves or a worktree is dirtied
during the last control run -> refused; happy path -> observations.final ==
observations.preflight and version-final is the last Lean call.

Scientific effect: NONE. This is an engineering guard on the runtime a
receipt describes; it raises no label, proves nothing and is not a review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
